  '2. …Ullal is a free, independent country with complete authority over itself, not under Portuguese rule. | 3. True (“Your Majesty, you will regret your stand.”) | 4. disobeyed | 5. C. (i), (iii) and (v) – bold, capable, determined',
  'II 1. Her mother would have felt comforted, proud and hopeful that her daughter would free Ullal.',
  '2. The people loved and trusted her; they were brave, patriotic and ready to sacrifice for freedom rather than live as a vassal.',
  '3. They must have felt overjoyed, proud, relieved and free at last.',
